"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzI3MzE4Mjcx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/crash","name":"crash","color":"885544","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-10-14T09:09:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10-15T11:29:40Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.6.dev1.official [8d8041bd4]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev1 - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 06 Oct 2025 18:48:29 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (nvidia; 580.95.05) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-12900K (24 threads) - 46.80 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nSince for each `*` in a glob expression the [`_wildcard_match`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e825169957e4ec67bc0baa6168af02b337399f6f/core/string/ustring.cpp#L3683) function recurses for each `*` in a glob expression, long enough patterns cause what I presume to be a stack overflow.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun\n\n```gdscript\n\"hihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihihi\".repeat(500000).match(\"*\".repeat(500000))\n```\n\nand watch the game crash.\nStrangely, I don't get an error message, the game window just closes.\nI'm pretty sure it's not a memory issue, since my memory usage only goes up by half a gigabyte or so.\n\nWhile people *probably* aren't running 2MB glob patterns on 36 MB strings, it *could* happen. The [Linux kernel](/linux/blob/master/lib/glob.c) uses an iterative approach which is dual-licensed under MIT and GPL and could possible be adapted.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSee above","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111634/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111634/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}